  "body": "- Disallow &lt;tfoot> before &lt;tbody> in the content model \n  \n  In HTML4, `tfoot` had to appear before `tbody`, but HTML5 allowed\n  either before or after. Placing it before causes problems for\n  keyboard focus order and order of accessibility objects, so this\n  changes the content model to no longer allow `tfoot` before `tbody`.\n  \n  Part of #352.\n- Fix #352: Change .tFoot and .createTFoot() to always insert at the end\n  \n  Since the content model no longer allows `tfoot` before `tbody`,\n  change these APIs to insert at the end. Firefox already does so,\n  which makes this seem reasonably safe to change.\n",
